{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/318424-vampire-four-corners-wod-forum-roleplay-no-player-limit","id":318424,"title":"Vampire: Four Corners; WoD forum roleplay, no player limit!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-21T12:51:28-08:00","id":318424,"title":"Vampire: Four Corners; WoD forum roleplay, no player limit!","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i53.photobucket.com/albums/g69/FallOutBoy66/Rockies_zpsce1e8595.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:26px\"><a href=\"http://vampirefourcorners.freeforums.net/\" target=\"_blank\">\u2022Home\u2022</a></span></b> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The four States of Utah, Colorado, New Mexico, and Arizona comprise the main Domains. The national parks and wastelands in between civilization are packed with Garou and other monstrous creatures even Kindred fear. The Capitals, Princedoms and Archbishoprics are almost constant warzones between the Camarilla, Sabbat, and Anarch ambitions vying in a massive power vacuum. Connected by the extensive highways and railroads of America\u2019s bygone industry, the Domains are a loose collection of allies and enemies. The Camarilla in the north hold stubbornly onto fragile footholds, while Sabbat in the south languish comfortably in their long-held territory, and the Anarchs fleeing from the ongoing Kuei-Jin conquest of California attempt to carve out Baronies every which where. The Nosferatu and Gangrel in particular are the most influential Clans in general due to frequent interstate travel among Kindred. The needs of certain Kindred to make eight hour drives to and fro population centers more often than not require special considerations, with Garou marauders lurking on the edges of towns and roads, at best, being among such concerns.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> While Vampires are the focus in Four Corners, Werewolves exist on the peripheries, and who knows what else beside\u2026<br /> <br /> --------------------------<br /> <br /> On this roleplay forum, we advocate both vampire <i>and </i>werewolf storylines, and host almost all of the clans and tribes. We are a brand new forum, and so the players that join now are those who will eventually help us shape the world and setting! We are a storytelling board for the most part, we pave the roads of our characters lives, and those will always intersect the paths of other characters. If you have any questions, please check us out, or message Cid, Atmosphere, or Darkness on the forums. Feel free to submit applications, we are fast to approve.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Note: We play by Vampire: The Masquerade and Werewolf: The Apocalypse guidelines, with a few adjustments to the metaplot.</span></span></div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4351,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4351-gabriel-folsom","user":"Gabriel Folsom","date":". 11-21-2014, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4351-gabriel-folsom","name":"Gabriel Folsom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}